                <pb facs="0365" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/434: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-26T10:00:00-04:00">April 26, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. I conveyed substance of Department’s telegram No. 36, April 25, 11 a.m., to
                    the Minister for Foreign Affairs yesterday evening at the same time leaving a
                    memorandum with him outlining representations made. The Minister stated that he
                    would endeavor at once to expedite a response from the Ministry of Finance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
